	affiliations = {Communication University of China, School of Economics and Management, Beijing, China},
	abstract = {Against the backdrop of the rapid global technological development, artificial intelligence (AI) serves as a core driving force for the productivity revolution. This paper, based on the data of Chinese Shanghai and Shenzhen A - share listed companies from 2011 to 2022, measures the level of corporate total factor productivity (TFP) and uses the double machine learning model to empirically examine the impact effect of corporate AI on TFP and its internal mechanism. The study finds that AI can significantly enhance the level of corporate TFP, and for every one - unit increase in AI, the TFP level of enterprises will increase by 3.6%. This conclusion still holds after a series of robustness and endogeneity tests. The results of the mechanism analysis show that AI can promote the development of TFP by enhancing enterprise digital transformation, innovation, human capital, and product competitiveness. The results of the heterogeneity analysis show that AI has a more obvious empowering effect on the TFP of non - polluting and high - tech industry enterprises; for technology - intensive and non - capital - intensive enterprises, the impact effect of AI on TFP is greater. Therefore, the government needs to strengthen the construction of AI infrastructure in the central and western regions, promote customized AI solutions, promote enterprise digital transformation, and provide policies such as technology transfer, financial subsidies, and tax incentives to comprehensively improve corporate total factor productivity. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
