	abstract = {Optimizing the management of construction processes is crucial in municipal engineering, yet it struggles with incorrect performance positioning. Traditional Neural network algorithms fail to adequately address this issue, resulting in subpar outcomes. Consequently, an optimized approach based on Computational intelligence for managing municipal engineering construction processes is introduced, and its efficacy is evaluated. Firstly, employing artificial intelligence theory helps identify influential factors, and these indicators are categorized according to the needs of process management optimization to minimize disruptive elements. Following this, a scheme for Computational intelligence-based construction process management optimization is devised using artificial intelligence theories, and its results are meticulously examined. MATLAB simulations indicate that, under specific evaluation criteria, Computational intelligence surpasses conventional Neural network algorithms in both precision and speed of impact variables in construction process management optimizationThis indicates that Computational intelligence can significantly enhance construction process management optimization in municipal engineering, leading to more efficient and effective project outcomes. The use of AI theory not only identifies the crucial factors influencing the construction process but also minimizes potential disruptions, ensuring a smoother execution of projects. This research paves the way for future exploration into integrating advanced algorithms with construction management practices. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
