	affiliations = {Utah Valley University, Orem, United States},
	abstract = {Management scholars suggest that project managers have the greatest influence on project success (Mansourimoayyed et al., 2020). The IT industry, compared to other industries, has been shown to be more prone to risk and project failures (The Standish Group International, 2020) and these failures are most commonly attributable to project management skills and techniques employed by the project managers (Project Management Institute, 2020). The Project Management Technology Quotient (PMTQ) is evolving to become a very valuable asset for organizations seeking digital competence and sustainability (Taboada et al., 2023). The Project Management Institute is also looking at practice-oriented project management through the utilization of emerging agile concepts and companies can take advantage of the efficiencies and transformative power of artificial intelligence to increase project success rates (Fridgeirsson et al., 2023). Not only is the use of AI application increasing efficiency by freeing project managers from tasks that can be automated, the use of AI is also seen by practitioners to enhance data-driven project management approaches which in turn improves the informational value. New applications are being explored in the field where some aspects can be automated while others will be augmented (Raisch & Krakowski, 2021). In fact, research has shown that not all aspects of project management are suitable for AI, simply because the tasks associated with these knowledge areas are tasks best done by humans (Fridgeirsson et al., 2023). This study explores a conceptual model for an AI-augment IT project management execution. The proposed model seeks to check and balance the implementation of AI techniques throughout an agile project management process within specific constraints set by the project manager. This proposed model will leverage the potential of technologies such as advanced digitalization, AI and big data, but deploying solutions for a more human